# Shortly — Project Structure

## Path Alias

- `@/` → `src/` (configured in `vite.config.js` + `jsconfig.json`).
- Always use `@/` for internal imports. Avoid deep relative paths (`../../../`).

## Directory Layout

```
src/
├── assets/                          # Static assets (images, fonts)
├── modules/                         # Feature modules (Vertical Slice mode)
│   ├── _core/                       #   Global shared layer (Feature-based mode)
│   │   ├── api/                     #     clients/ errors/ hooks/ utils/
│   │   ├── components/              #     atom/ base/ composite/ design/ layout/
│   │   ├── constants/ context/ hooks/ layouts/ pages/ stores/ utils/
│   │   └── index.js
│   │
│   ├── Pattern: <module>/
│   │   ├── _shared/                 #   Slice-shared (api/ constants/ contexts/ hooks/ stores/)
│   │   ├── features/<slice>/        #   One dir per use case (api/ components/ validators/)
│   │   ├── layouts/                 #   Module layout components
│   │   ├── pages/                   #   Module page components
│   │   └── index.js                 #   Public API
│   │
│   ├── auth/                        #   login/ register/ session/
│   ├── links/                       #   shortener/ management/
│   ├── brand/                       #   marketing/ (no _shared/ or layouts/)
│   └── settings/                    #   profile/ (no layouts/)
│
├── router/                          # AppRouter.jsx, ProtectedRoute.jsx
├── App.jsx
├── index.css                        # Tailwind v4 entry + DaisyUI themes
└── main.jsx
```

## Module Architecture Mode: Vertical Slice

**Detection:** Modules under `src/modules/` contain `features/<slice>/` directories (e.g., `auth/features/login/`, `links/features/shortener/`).

**Project-specific exceptions:**
- `brand/` has no `_shared/` (only one slice: `marketing/`)
- `settings/` has `_shared/` but no `layouts/`

For detailed structure rules, execution steps, and Feature-based vs Vertical Slice decision guide, load the [`module-architecture`](/shortly/.agents/skills/module-architecture/SKILL.md) skill.

> The tree view above shows the Vertical Slice pattern. The skill has the full reference.

## Cross-Module Dependency Rules

| From ↓ \ To → | `_core/` | Other modules |
|---|---|---|
| **`_core/`** | ✅ Allowed | ❌ Forbidden (core has no business logic) |
| **Module A** | ✅ Allowed | ❌ Forbidden (must go through `index.js` exports) |
| **Module slice** | ✅ Allowed | ❌ Forbidden (ditto) |

- Modules expose their public API via root `index.js`. Other modules cannot deep-import into a module's internals.
- If two feature modules need the same thing, it goes in `_core/`.

## Critical Conventions

| Convention | Rule |
|---|---|
| **Folder naming** | kebab-case for directories |
| **Component naming** | PascalCase, prefix with Type: `[A\|B\|C\|D\|L][ComponentName]` |
| **Hook/utility naming** | camelCase, prefixed with `use-` for hooks |
| **File naming** | kebab-case, matches the exported name (e.g., `use-session.js` → `useSession`) |
| **Exports** | One component/function per file. Named exports only (no `export default`). |
| **Pages/Layouts** | Always at module root — never inside a slice or `_shared/` |
| **Module API** | Each module has `index.js` that re-exports the public contract |

